60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B seems the most natural, but it might lead to more ""bike-shoving"" if the racks are crowded.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I worry that Option B might make the morning rush even more stressful. A lottery might be more peaceful.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that makes sense. It solves the fairness issue and finally puts some money in the account.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"Option B is the most sustainable. No billing, no lists, no monthly tracking. It removes the administrative burden entirely.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option C! A lottery is the only way to be 100% fair! Everyone gets a chance, and no one can complain about favoritism!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a lottery could be frustrating. Imagine the tension when one person wins a spot three years in a row.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"That is true. But Option A feels a bit cold, doesn't it? Charging our neighbors for a place to put their bike...","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"It's not ""cold,"" Shizue, it's professional. It's how the rest of the world works. Plus, the building needs the funds.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, the ""professional"" approach is exactly what leads to burnout. I've seen it happen twice already in this building.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,But Option B is just the same as now! People will still hog the best spots or block others. We need a rule!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we go with Option C, we might see people resenting each other based on the luck of the draw.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I just want the mornings to be calm. If we have a lottery, people might feel they ""own"" their spot and be more careful.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,Let's be honest: people value what they pay for. Option A ensures that only those who truly need the space will take it.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,I cannot support Option A. The monthly reconciliation is too much. Option B is the only one that doesn't create a new job.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I can't support Option B! It's just ""survival of the fittest."" A lottery is the only way to break the cycle of favoritism!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I'll vote for Option B. It's the least likely to create a rigid hierarchy or a sense of ""winning and losing"" among us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I think I will go with Option C. It gives everyone a fair chance and might stop the morning shoving matches.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'm sticking with Option A. It's the most pragmatic and beneficial for the building's long-term financial health.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,I'm voting for Option B. It's the only choice that is truly sustainable for the person managing the association.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm definitely voting for Option C! Let's make it a game and give everyone an equal shot at the best spots!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
